[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "Kestrel Manufacturing — June 2025 Inventory Tie-Out: Accrual Policy Note & Vendor Credit Memo Summary",
  "path": "engagements/kestrel-manufacturing/inventory/june-2025-accrual-reconciliation-summary.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "Kestrel Manufacturing — June 2025 Inventory Tie-Out"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Accrual Policy Note & Vendor Credit Memo — Reconciliation Findings"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared by: Nadia Osman, Staff Accountant | Date: [current date] | For: Gabriel, Theo, Victor"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. Purpose"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This summary documents the findings from the June 2025 inventory accrual tie-out for Kestrel Manufacturing. The work focused on two items: (a) confirming the accrual policy note for June aligns with the 2025 accrual policy, and (b) locating and applying the vendor credit memo to the June inventory accrual balance."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Accrual Policy Note — 2025 Policy"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The 2025 accrual policy note (referenced in the Kestrel file as 'Kestrel_Accrual_Policy_2025.pdf') requires that inventory-related accruals be recorded when goods are received but not yet invoiced, using the vendor's most recent pricing or the standard cost where pricing is unavailable. Accruals must be reversed in the subsequent month upon invoice receipt."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Policy Element", "Requirement", "June 2025 Application"],
        "rows": [
          ["Timing of accrual", "Goods received, not invoiced (GRNI)", "Accrual booked June 30 for received goods"],
          ["Valuation basis", "Latest vendor price or standard cost", "Standard cost used — vendor pricing unavailable"],
          ["Reversal", "Reversed next month on invoice", "Reversal scheduled for July invoice posting"],
          ["Documentation", "Supporting receipt and PO reference", "PO #K-2214 and receiving report #RR-1067 on file"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The June 2025 accrual policy note was reviewed against the 2025 policy. The June note is consistent with the policy; no deviations were identified."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Vendor Credit Memo — Application to June Inventory Accrual"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The vendor credit memo (reference CM-8842, dated June 18, 2025, from Metalworks Supply Co.) was located and reviewed. The credit memo relates to overbilling on PO #K-2214 for steel components received in May 2025, amounting to $4,850.00."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The credit memo was applied against the June 2025 inventory accrual balance, reducing the accrual by $4,850.00. The adjusted accrual balance as of June 30, 2025, is presented below."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Item", "Amount (USD)"],
        "rows": [
          ["Gross inventory accrual (June 30)", "128,420.00"],
          ["Less: Vendor credit memo CM-8842", "(4,850.00)"],
          ["Net inventory accrual (June 30)", "123,570.00"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Reconciliation Notes"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "The gross accrual of $128,420.00 ties to the June inventory subledger for GRNI items under PO #K-2214 and PO #K-2218.",
          "The credit memo was posted to the general ledger on June 25, 2025; the tie-out confirms the posting was captured in the June accrual balance before adjustment.",
          "No additional credit memos or unapplied credits were identified for the June period.",
          "The net accrual of $123,570.00 will be reversed in July upon receipt of the July invoices, per the 2025 accrual policy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Conclusion & Next Steps"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The June 2025 inventory accrual tie-out is complete. The accrual policy note is compliant with the 2025 policy, and the vendor credit memo has been correctly applied. No further adjustments are required for the June close."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Next steps: (1) Monitor July invoices to confirm the reversal posts correctly; (2) Share this summary with Gabriel and Theo for the Q3 margin driver discussion; (3) File the credit memo and policy note in the Kestrel workpaper binder."
      }
    ]
  }
}
